      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "1. Start by simplifying the left side of the expression $(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)$.\n2. Recognize that the angles $20^\\circ$ and $25^\\circ$ are related through their complementary angles, i.e., $65^\\circ$.\n3. Recall the tangent addition formula: $\\tan (A + B) = \\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A \\tan B}$.\n4. Apply the formula to $\\tan (65^\\circ)$:\n   \\[\n   \\tan 65^\\circ = \\tan (45^\\circ + 20^\\circ) = \\frac{\\tan 45^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 45^\\circ \\tan 20^\\circ} = \\frac{1 + \\tan 20^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ}.\n   \\]\n5. Substitute $\\tan 65^\\circ$ back into the product:\n   \\[\n   (1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = (1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)\\left(1 + \\frac{1 + \\tan 20^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ}\\right).\n   \\]\n6. Simplify the expression inside the parentheses:\n   \\[\n   1 + \\frac{1 + \\tan 20^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ} = \\frac{(1 - \\tan 20^\\circ) + (1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ} = \\frac{2}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ}.\n   \\]\n7. Therefore, the original expression becomes:\n   \\[\n   (1 + \\tan 20^\\circ) \\cdot \\frac{2}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ}.\n   \\]\n8. Recognize that $1 - \\tan 20^\\circ = \\tan 70^\\circ$ (since $\\tan (90^\\circ - \\theta) = \\cot \\theta$):\n   \\[\n   (1 + \\tan 20^\\circ) \\cdot \\frac{2}{\\tan 70^\\circ} = 2 + 2 \\tan 20^\\circ.\n   \\]\n9. Since $\\tan 20^\\circ \\approx 0.36397$, we have:\n   \\[\n   2 + 2 \\cdot 0.36397 = 2 + 0.72794 = 2.72794.\n   \\]\n10. The exact value of $\\tan 20^\\circ$ is not needed for simplification of this specific problem as it cancels out in the final steps. Thus, the simplified form of the given expression is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{4}.\n   \\]",
