      "text": "To simplify \\((1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)\\), we start by using the tangent addition formula. Recall that \\(\\tan(A + B) = \\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A \\tan B}\\). Setting \\(A = 20^\\circ\\) and \\(B = 25^\\circ\\), we have:\n\n\\[\n\\tan(45^\\circ) = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\tan 45^\\circ = 1\\), we get:\n\n\\[\n1 = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nThis can be rearranged to:\n\n\\[\n1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\n\nAdding 1 to both sides, we get:\n\n\\[\n1 + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = 1\n\\]\n\nor equivalently,\n\n\\[\n1 + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ + (\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1\n\\]\n\nSo,\n\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ = 0\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = -(\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ)\n\\]\n\nNow, substituting this back into the original expression, we have:\n\n\\[\n(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = (1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + (-\\tan 20^\\circ - \\tan 25^\\circ)) = (1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 - (\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ))\n\\]\n\nUsing the identity above, we simplify further:\n\n\\[\n(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 - (\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ)) = (1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 - \\tan 20^\\circ - \\tan 25^\\circ)\n\\]\n\nThis is exactly the same expression we squared in our rearrangement. Therefore, we have:\n\n\\[\n(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1\n\\]\n\nSo, the simplified value is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]",
