      "text": "To simplify \\((1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)\\), we start by using the tangent addition formula. The tangent addition formula states that \\(\\tan(A + B) = \\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A \\tan B}\\).\n\nFirst, let \\(A = 20^\\circ\\) and \\(B = 25^\\circ\\). Then we have:\n\\[\n\\tan(20^\\circ + 25^\\circ) = \\tan 45^\\circ\n\\]\nWe know that \\(\\tan 45^\\circ = 1\\). Therefore,\n\\[\n\\tan(20^\\circ + 25^\\circ) = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ} = 1\n\\]\nThis implies:\n\\[\n\\tan 45^\\circ = 1 = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ}\n\\]\nCross-multiplying gives:\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ = 1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nRearranging terms, we get:\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = 1\n\\]\nNow, we use this identity to simplify the original expression. Let \\(x = \\tan 20^\\circ\\) and \\(y = \\tan 25^\\circ\\). Then \\(xy = -1\\) (since \\(\\tan(20^\\circ + 25^\\circ) = 1\\) implies \\(\\tan 45^\\circ = 1 = \\frac{x + y}{1 - xy}\\) and \\(-(-1) = 1\\)). We need to simplify:\n\\[\n(1 + x)(1 + y) = 1 + x + y + xy\n\\]\nSubstituting \\(xy = -1\\) into the expression, we get:\n\\[\n1 + x + y + xy = 1 + x + y - 1 = x + y\n\\]\nfrom the identity \\(\\tan 45^\\circ = 1 = \\frac{x + y}{1 - xy}\\) and knowing \\(xy = -1\\), so:\n\\[\n1 + x + y + xy = 1 + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ - 1 = \\tan 45^\\circ = 1\n\\]\nThus, the simplified value of \\((1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
